<h1>The Charter</h1>
<p class="lede">The <a href="/manifesto/">manifesto</a> says what we believe. This is what it means in practice.</p>
<div class="notice">
  <p><strong>JRCv1 is a draft conformance standard, not a copyright licence.</strong> It hasn't been legally reviewed, and nothing about it is OSI-approved. A project meets it by publishing evidence, not by paying anyone or asking permission. Disagree with a requirement? <a href="{{ repoUrl }}/issues/new?template=charter-rfc.md">Open an RFC</a>.</p>
</div>
